{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target += normal_lpdf(delta | 0, 3)` prior with the algebraically equivalent built-in prior `delta_free ~ multi_normal_prec(...)` on the free sum-to-zero item parameters. Reordered parameter priors so that `lambda_adj` and `sigma` are observed before they are used in the conditional prior for `theta`, and `delta_free` is observed before `delta` is used in the likelihood. The likelihood for protected data remains the single top-level statement `y ~ bernoulli_logit(theta[jj] - delta[ii])`. The supplied data were not changed. The generated-quantities calculation for `lambda` was guarded for `K == 1` to avoid an out-of-range empty-tail slice while preserving the original formula for `K > 1` and not changing the posterior/log density.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  matrix obtain_adjustments(matrix W) {
    real min_w;
    real max_w;
    int minmax_count;
    matrix[2, cols(W)] adj;
    adj[1, 1] = 0;
    adj[2, 1] = 1;
    if(cols(W) > 1) {
      for(k in 2:cols(W)) {                       // remaining columns
        min_w = min(W[1:rows(W), k]);
        max_w = max(W[1:rows(W), k]);
        minmax_count = 0;
        for(j in 1:rows(W))
          minmax_count = minmax_count + W[j,k] == min_w || W[j,k] == max_w;
        if(minmax_count == rows(W)) {       // if column takes only 2 values
          adj[1, k] = mean(W[1:rows(W), k]);
          adj[2, k] = (max_w - min_w);
        } else {                            // if column takes > 2 values
          adj[1, k] = mean(W[1:rows(W), k]);
          adj[2, k] = sd(W[1:rows(W), k]) * 2;
        }
      }
    }
    return adj;
  }
}
data {
  int<lower=1> I;               // // questions
  int<lower=1> J;               // // persons
  int<lower=1> N;               // // observations
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=I> ii;  // question for n
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> jj;  // person for n
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;   // correctness for n
  int<lower=1> K;               // // person covariates
  matrix[J,K] W;                // person covariate matrix
}
transformed data {
  matrix[2,K] adj;               // values for centering and scaling covariates
  matrix[J,K] W_adj;             // centered and scaled covariates
  vector[I - 1] delta_free_prior_mean;
  matrix[I - 1, I - 1] delta_free_prior_precision;
  adj = obtain_adjustments(W);
  for(k in 1:K) for(j in 1:J)
      W_adj[j,k] = (W[j,k] - adj[1,k]) / adj[2,k];
  delta_free_prior_mean = rep_vector(0.0, I - 1);
  delta_free_prior_precision = (diag_matrix(rep_vector(1.0, I - 1)) + rep_matrix(1.0, I - 1, I - 1)) / 9.0;
}
parameters {
  vector[I-1] delta_free;
  vector[J] theta;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
  vector[K] lambda_adj;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[I] delta;
  delta[1:(I-1)] = delta_free;
  delta[I] = -1*sum(delta_free);
}
model {
  lambda_adj ~ student_t(3, 0, 1);
  sigma ~ exponential(.1);
  theta ~ normal(W_adj*lambda_adj, sigma);
  delta_free ~ multi_normal_prec(delta_free_prior_mean, delta_free_prior_precision);
  y ~ bernoulli_logit(theta[jj] - delta[ii]);
}
generated quantities {
  vector[K] lambda;
  vector[J] theta_fix;
  vector[J] zeta;
  if (K > 1) {
    lambda[2:K] = lambda_adj[2:K] ./ to_vector(adj[2,2:K]);
    lambda[1] = W_adj[1, 1:K]*lambda_adj[1:K] - W[1, 2:K]*lambda[2:K];
  } else {
    lambda[1] = W_adj[1, 1]*lambda_adj[1];
  }
  theta_fix = W_adj*lambda_adj;
  zeta = theta - theta_fix;
}
","data_safe_json":"{"I":3,"J":4,"K":1,"N":5,"W":[[4.163684310615883],[3.167589221544227],[5.322881817251204],[4.088129694518081]],"ii":[3,1,3,2,2],"jj":[1,4,2,4,3],"y":[1,1,0,0,0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
